			"original_statement": "The term 'eschatology' originates from the Greek words 'eschatos' meaning 'last' and 'logos' meaning 'study' or 'word', thus literally translating to 'the study of the last things'. Historically, it has been used to refer to theological interpretations concerning the ultimate destiny of the world and mankind."
